    <bpmn:process id="W_W595" name="W595. ERP System Daily Health Check &amp; Integration Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily scheduled health check (automated at 05:00); real-time integration failure alert from W380
Frequency: Daily automated health check at 05:00 (before store operations begin at 08:00); continuous real-time integration monitoring 24/7
Volume: 1 unified ERP system; 600 POS terminals across 200 stores; 4 WMS instances; 1 ecommerce platform; BIR eFPS/EIS integration; bank integrations (BDO, BPI, Metrobank, Chinabank); payment gateways (GCash, PayMaya, credit card processors); ~15–20 critical integration endpoints monitored continuously
Owner: ERP System Administrator
Participants: ERP System Administrator, IT Infrastructure Engineer (R for network/server issues), IT Helpdesk Lead (R for user communication), Integration Specialist (R for API issues), CIO (A for escalation)
Source: workflow W595 — ERP System Daily Health Check &amp; Integration Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W595_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W595_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W595_Lane2" name="ERP System Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W595_Lane3" name="Integration Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W595_End20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W595_Start5" name="Daily scheduled health check (automated at 05:00); real-time integration failure alert…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task6" name="Overnight batch job completion verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Overnight batch job completion verification: system runs automated check of all overnight batch jobs — (a) batch job status: completed, completed with warnings, failed; (b) critical batch jobs verified: payroll calculation (W10), inventory reconciliation (W6/W42), demand forecast recalculation (W31), store replenishment order generation (W4), POS transaction settlement and posting (W525), ecommerce order import and inventory sync, AP aging refresh (W7), AR posting and collection update (W8), GL consolidation across 5 entities (W9), warehouse replenishment wave planning; (c) for any failed job: system captures error log, job step that failed, data scope affected, and recommended retry action; (d) results pushed to ERP System Administrator dashboard and mobile notification by 05:15
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (05:00–05:15)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task7" name="ERP System Administrator reviews batch job results">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: ERP System Administrator reviews batch job results: Administrator reviews dashboard at 05:30 — (a) if all critical jobs completed successfully: proceed to integration checks (step 3); (b) if non-critical job failed (e.g., historical data archiving, analytics cube refresh): log in W48 ticket for resolution during business hours, proceed to integration checks; (c) if critical job failed: assess impact — which business processes are affected, how many stores, what data is stale; trigger immediate remediation: (i) retry failed job, (ii) if retry fails: escalate to IT Infrastructure Engineer for server/database investigation, (iii) if data integrity at risk: escalate to CIO for decision on manual workaround vs. delayed store opening; communicate to affected business stakeholders by 06:30
Responsible (R): ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): CIO (for critical failures)
Duration: 15–30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task8" name="Integration connectivity check — POS-to-ERP">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Integration connectivity check — POS-to-ERP: system pings all 600 POS terminal connections and verifies — (a) real-time connectivity status: online terminals vs. offline terminals; (b) last successful transaction sync timestamp per terminal; (c) offline mode terminals per W5G — count, duration of offline, pending transaction count; (d) POS terminal software version compliance: are all terminals running the current POS software version?; (e) for terminals offline &gt;4 hours: generate W48 ticket for IT Field Support investigation (may indicate network issue at store per W366); results summary: X/600 terminals online, Y terminals in offline mode with Z pending transactions
Responsible (R): System / ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): IT Helpdesk Lead
Duration: 10 min/day (review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task9" name="Integration connectivity check — ERP-to-WMS">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Integration connectivity check — ERP-to-WMS: system verifies connection to all 4 WMS instances (1 per DC) — (a) API health: ping response time &lt;2 seconds (threshold); (b) inbound/outbound document sync: verify Transfer Orders (W22), PO receipts (W3), pick wave confirmations (W4) are flowing; (c) data synchronization lag: time difference between ERP last update and WMS last update — acceptable threshold &lt;15 minutes; (d) if sync lag &gt;15 minutes at any DC: investigate — common causes: WMS server load, network latency, API timeout; escalate to DC IT if local issue; (e) verify ASN (Advanced Shipping Notice) generation for outbound orders in queue
Responsible (R): System / ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Engineer
Duration: 10 min/day (review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task10" name="Integration connectivity check — ERP-to-ecommerce">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Integration connectivity check — ERP-to-ecommerce: system verifies ecommerce platform integration — (a) product catalog sync: verify latest price changes (W40) and inventory levels are reflected on ecommerce site; (b) order import: verify new ecommerce orders are importing into ERP as Sales Orders without errors; (c) inventory sync: verify ERP available-to-promise (ATP) quantities match ecommerce displayed stock; (d) payment gateway reconciliation: verify GCash, PayMaya, and credit card settlement files from previous day are received and matched; (e) for any sync failure: check integration middleware logs per W257, identify failed transactions, retry or manually post
Responsible (R): System / ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): Integration Specialist
Duration: 10 min/day (review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task11" name="Integration connectivity check — ERP-to-BIR">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Integration connectivity check — ERP-to-BIR: system verifies BIR integration endpoints — (a) eFPS connectivity: verify tax filing module can connect to BIR eFPS portal (filing happens monthly but connectivity should be verified daily); (b) EIS (Electronic Invoicing/Receipting): verify sales data transmission pipeline is active — BIR requires real-time or near-real-time transmission of sales data per TRAIN law and CREATE law requirements; (c) if EIS transmission queue has failed transactions: investigate and retry before 08:00 to avoid BIR compliance risk
Responsible (R): System / ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/day (review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task12" name="Integration connectivity check — ERP-to-banks">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Integration connectivity check — ERP-to-banks: system verifies bank integration endpoints — (a) BDO, BPI, Metrobank, Chinabank file transmission: verify previous day&#x27;s bank files (AP payment files per W556, payroll credit files per W10, collection files per W8) were successfully transmitted and acknowledged by bank; (b) bank statement auto-import: verify today&#x27;s bank statement files are available and imported for cash position per W30; (c) GCash/PayMaya settlement reconciliation: verify digital wallet settlement files from previous day are received and reconciled; (d) for any failed transmission: check SFTP connectivity, file format compliance, and bank system status; retransmit if needed
Responsible (R): System / ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: 10 min/day (review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task13" name="Data synchronization lag check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Data synchronization lag check: system generates consolidated sync lag report across all integration endpoints — (a) POS-to-ERP: max lag across 600 terminals (target: &lt;5 min for online terminals); (b) ERP-to-WMS: lag per DC (target: &lt;15 min); (c) ERP-to-ecommerce: catalog and inventory sync lag (target: &lt;30 min for inventory, &lt;2 hours for catalog changes); (d) overall data freshness score: weighted composite of all integration lags — green (&lt;5 min avg lag), amber (5–15 min), red (&gt;15 min); (e) persistent lag at any endpoint triggers W380 alert with severity classification
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task14" name="Error queue review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Error queue review: Administrator reviews error queues across all integration endpoints — (a) failed POS transactions in retry queue: count, age of oldest failed transaction, store distribution; (b) failed WMS document postings: count, affected DC, document types; (c) failed ecommerce order imports: count, error type (payment failure, inventory mismatch, duplicate order); (d) failed bank file transmissions: count, bank, file type; (e) failed BIR data submissions: count, submission type; (f) for each error category: Administrator applies standard remediation (retry, manual correction, escalate per W48) and targets clearing all queues before 07:30
Responsible (R): ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): IT Helpdesk Lead
Duration: 20–30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task15" name="Performance metrics review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Performance metrics review: system generates daily ERP performance snapshot — (a) database response time: average query execution time (target: &lt;500ms for standard queries); (b) batch processing duration: total overnight batch window vs. target window (target: complete by 05:00); (c) API response time: average response time per integration endpoint; (d) server resource utilization: CPU, memory, disk I/O across ERP application and database servers (target: &lt;70% peak utilization during business hours); (e) concurrent user sessions: peak sessions previous day vs. capacity threshold; (f) if any metric exceeds threshold for 3 consecutive days: generate W376 capacity alert for IT Infrastructure review
Responsible (R): System / ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Engineer
Duration: 10 min/day (review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task16" name="Health check report generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Health check report generation: by 07:00, system compiles all checks into a single Daily Health Check Report — (a) executive summary: green/amber/red status for each integration domain (POS, WMS, ecommerce, BIR, banking, core ERP); (b) batch job summary: completed/failed/retry counts; (c) integration connectivity: online/offline counts per domain; (d) sync lag: composite score and individual endpoint scores; (e) error queue: open errors by category with aging; (f) performance: key metrics vs. thresholds; (g) action items: unresolved issues requiring attention during business hours; report distributed to: CIO, IT Helpdesk Lead, Integration Specialist, IT Infrastructure Engineer
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (07:00)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task17" name="Issue escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Issue escalation: for any red-status items identified in the health check — (a) P1 escalation (per W48 severity matrix): system-down integration failure affecting revenue (e.g., all POS offline, ecommerce down, WMS failure at a DC) — immediate CIO notification, activate incident response per W48; (b) P2 escalation: major integration degradation (e.g., one bank file transmission failed, WMS sync lag &gt;30 min, BIR EIS queue backup) — IT Helpdesk Lead notified, target resolution within 8 hours; (c) P3 escalation: non-critical issues (e.g., non-critical batch job failure, single POS terminal offline, performance metric approaching threshold) — logged in W48, resolved within 24 hours
Responsible (R): ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 5–10 min/day (escalation actions)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow35</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W595_Task18" name="Weekly health trend review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 13: Weekly health trend review: every Monday, ERP System Administrator compiles weekly health trend for IT team meeting — (a) batch job success rate: daily % for the week, any recurring failures; (b) integration uptime: uptime % per endpoint for the week; (c) error queue volume trend: daily open errors and clearance rate; (d) performance metrics trend: key metrics plotted daily for the week; (e) top 5 recurring issues with root cause classification; (f) comparison to previous week and same week last year; (g) feed into W376 capacity planning and W378 problem management for systemic issues
Responsible (R): ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow35</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow36</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W595_Task19" name="Monthly integration health SLA report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 14: Monthly integration health SLA report: Integration Specialist compiles monthly SLA report for CIO — (a) integration availability SLA: target 99.5% uptime per endpoint; actual vs. target by endpoint; (b) data sync SLA: % of time all endpoints within lag threshold; (c) batch completion SLA: % of days all critical jobs completed before 05:00; (d) incident impact: number and duration of integration-related P1/P2 incidents; (e) planned maintenance windows: scheduled downtime vs. actual; (f) feed into W55 DR testing schedule and W257 API lifecycle review
Responsible (R): Integration Specialist
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 3–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow36</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W595_Flow37</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W595_End20" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W595_Flow37</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W595_Annotation21">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: W55 DR plan, W382 backup operations, high-availability clustering, and the daily health check to catch degradation before failure; operational: W376 capacity planning, database optimization, and batch job parallelization; operational: consolidated health check dashboard (step 11) and cross-training of IT team
Owner: ERP System Administrator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
