    <bpmn:process id="W_W614" name="W614. Data Warehouse &amp; ETL Pipeline Daily Operations &amp; Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Start of business day; ETL pipeline scheduled execution; pipeline failure alert
Frequency: Daily monitoring; 24/7 automated pipeline execution
Volume: ~93,000 POS transactions/day (~2.8M/month); ~1,400 ecommerce orders/day; ~18,000 PO lines/month; ~9,500 AP invoices/month; plus HR, inventory, and master data feeds
Owner: BI/Data Engineer
Participants: BI/Data Engineer, Database Administrator, IT Integration Specialist, BI Analyst, business data stewards
Source: workflow W614 — Data Warehouse &amp; ETL Pipeline Daily Operations &amp; Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W614_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W614_Lane1" name="BI">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W614_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W614_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W614_Start4" name="Start of business day; ETL pipeline scheduled execution; pipeline failure alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W614_Task5" name="Morning (6:00 AM): BI/Data Engineer reviews overnight ETL pipeline execution…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning (6:00 AM): BI/Data Engineer reviews overnight ETL pipeline execution dashboard — all scheduled jobs (POS transaction load, inventory snapshot, AP/AR sync, HR attendance feed, ecommerce order sync, master data replication) with status (Success, Warning, Failed, Running)
Responsible (R): BI/Data Engineer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W614_Task6" name="For failed jobs: BI/Data Engineer investigates error logs — common causes: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: For failed jobs: BI/Data Engineer investigates error logs — common causes: (a) source system unavailable (POS store offline, ecommerce API timeout), (b) data format change (vendor updated API response), (c) resource contention (database lock, storage full), (d) data quality exception (null values in required fields, duplicate records)
Responsible (R): BI/Data Engineer
Accountable (A): Database Administrator
Duration: 15-60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W614_Task7" name="BI/Data Engineer re-executes failed jobs after root cause resolution; validates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: BI/Data Engineer re-executes failed jobs after root cause resolution; validates data completeness by comparing source record counts to data warehouse load counts; system auto-logs reconciliation results
Responsible (R): BI/Data Engineer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W614_Task8" name="Data quality monitoring: system runs automated data quality checks on critical…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Data quality monitoring: system runs automated data quality checks on critical dimensions — (a) completeness (% of required fields populated), (b) uniqueness (duplicate detection on key business keys), (c) timeliness (data freshness vs. SLA), (d) consistency (cross-system referential integrity)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W614_Task9" name="Data quality exceptions auto-route to data stewards per domain: merchandise…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Data quality exceptions auto-route to data stewards per domain: merchandise data quality issues → Category Manager, customer data quality → CRM Manager, financial data quality → Controller, inventory data quality → Supply Planning Manager
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): BI/Data Engineer
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W614_Task10" name="Mid-day: BI/Data Engineer reviews real-time streaming pipeline health — POS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Mid-day: BI/Data Engineer reviews real-time streaming pipeline health — POS event stream (per W533), inventory deduction stream, ecommerce order stream; monitors message queue depth, processing latency, and consumer lag
Responsible (R): BI/Data Engineer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W614_Task11" name="End of day: system generates daily ETL operations report — pipeline execution…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: End of day: system generates daily ETL operations report — pipeline execution summary, data quality scores, record counts by source, latency metrics, and storage utilization; BI/Data Engineer reviews and files issues for weekly review
Responsible (R): System / BI/Data Engineer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W614_Task12" name="Weekly: BI/Data Engineer and Database Administrator conduct pipeline…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly: BI/Data Engineer and Database Administrator conduct pipeline performance review — identify slow-running transformations, optimize queries, adjust resource allocation, plan capacity for upcoming data volume growth
Responsible (R): BI/Data Engineer
Accountable (A): Database Administrator
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W614_Task13" name="Monthly: BI/Data Engineer presents data platform health report to IT leadership…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Monthly: BI/Data Engineer presents data platform health report to IT leadership and business stakeholders — data warehouse availability, data quality trends, pipeline performance, storage growth forecast, and upcoming enhancements
Responsible (R): BI/Data Engineer
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W614_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W614_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W614_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W614_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: dependency visualization, independent job retry, and data warehouse snapshot isolation; operational: daily data quality scoring with trend monitoring and threshold-based escalation; operational: data archiving strategy (per W396) and tiered storage
Owner: BI/Data Engineer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
