    <bpmn:process id="W_W734" name="W734. Data Quality Daily Triage &amp; Remediation Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Start of IT operations day; or automated data quality alert from monitoring system
Frequency: Daily review; continuous automated monitoring
Volume: ~50–100 data quality alerts/day across all master data domains
Owner: Data Steward
Participants: IT Integration Manager, Master Data Analyst, Business User (data owner)
Source: workflow W734 — Data Quality Daily Triage &amp; Remediation Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W734_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W734_Lane1" name="Data Steward">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W734_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W734_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W734_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W734_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W734_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W734_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W734_Start3" name="Start of IT operations day; or automated data quality alert from monitoring system">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W734_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W734_Task4" name="Morning data quality dashboard review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning data quality dashboard review: Data Steward reviews data quality dashboard: (a) overnight automated data quality checks: (i) item master: missing attributes (UOM, weight, dimensions, category), duplicate barcodes, inactive SKUs with open POs, negative inventory items; (ii) customer master: incomplete records (missing email, phone, address), duplicate records per W253, dormant accounts per W560; (iii) vendor master: missing TIN per W732, incomplete banking details, expired certifications; (iv) financial master: uncategorized GL entries, orphan cost centers, unbalanced intercompany entries; (v) employee master: missing statutory IDs per W292, incorrect entity assignment; (b) prioritize issues by business impact: (i) Critical: data errors affecting POS pricing (wrong price shown to customer), AP matching (3-way match failure), payroll (incorrect deductions); (ii) High: data errors affecting inventory accuracy, ecommerce catalog, reporting; (iii) Medium: data quality issues affecting analytics, planning; (iv) Low: cosmetic data issues (formatting, naming conventions)
Responsible (R): Data Steward
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 20-30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W734_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W734_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W734_Task5" name="Critical issue immediate remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Critical issue immediate remediation: for Critical-priority issues: (a) identify root cause: system integration error, manual data entry mistake, master data change without validation per W252; (b) correct data in source system: (i) item master corrections per W252 governance; (ii) customer master corrections per W253; (iii) vendor master corrections per W287; (c) propagate correction: (i) if item price was wrong: force price push to POS per POS-042 real-time sync; (ii) if inventory count was wrong: adjust per W92 and update ecommerce ATP; (iii) if AP matching data was wrong: re-trigger 3-way match per W7; (d) notify affected business users of correction and any downstream impact; (e) document remediation in data quality log
Responsible (R): Data Steward
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 15-30 min per critical issue</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W734_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W734_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W734_Task6" name="Batch remediation for High-priority issues">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Batch remediation for High-priority issues: for High-priority issues that are not time-critical: (a) group similar issues for batch remediation: (i) missing product attributes in a category → assign to Merchandising for batch update; (ii) duplicate customer records → merge per W619; (iii) incomplete vendor records → assign to Procurement for vendor outreach; (b) assign remediation tasks to data owners with deadline; (c) track remediation progress in data quality queue
Responsible (R): Data Steward
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30-60 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W734_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W734_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W734_Task7" name="Data quality trend reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Data quality trend reporting: weekly, Data Steward reports: (a) total data quality issues by domain and severity; (b) resolution rate: issues opened vs. closed per week; (c) aging: issues open &gt;7 days, &gt;30 days; (d) root cause analysis: systemic issues vs. one-time errors; (e) data quality score by domain: target &gt;98% for item, customer, and vendor master; (f) recommendations for process or system improvements to prevent recurring issues
Responsible (R): Data Steward
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W734_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W734_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W734_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W734_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W734_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: Data Steward review and approval gate
Owner: Data Steward</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W734_Assoc10" sourceRef="W734_Annotation9" targetRef="W734_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W734_Flow11" sourceRef="W734_Start3" targetRef="W734_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W734_Flow12" sourceRef="W734_Task4" targetRef="W734_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W734_Flow13" sourceRef="W734_Task5" targetRef="W734_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W734_Flow14" sourceRef="W734_Task6" targetRef="W734_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W734_Flow15" sourceRef="W734_Task7" targetRef="W734_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
