    <bpmn:process id="W_W787" name="W787. ERP System Monthly Performance Review &amp; Capacity Planning Update" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly IT operations review cycle
Frequency: Monthly review; quarterly capacity planning update
Volume: 1 ERP system + all integrations across 205 locations
Owner: IT Infrastructure Manager
Participants: IT Infrastructure Manager, ERP Administrator, Database Administrator, CIO
Source: workflow W787 — ERP System Monthly Performance Review &amp; Capacity Planning Update</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W787_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W787_Lane1" name="ERP Admin">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W787_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W787_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W787_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W787_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W787_Lane2" name="IT Infra Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W787_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W787_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W787_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W787_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W787_Start4" name="Monthly IT operations review cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W787_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W787_Task5" name="Monthly performance data compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly performance data compilation: ERP Administrator compiles: (a) system uptime by module (POS, ecommerce, WMS, AP/AR, HR), (b) average response time by transaction type (POS sale, inventory query, report generation, API call), (c) peak concurrent users and peak transaction throughput, (d) batch job completion times (month-end close, nightly reconciliation per W525, payroll per W10), (e) database growth (storage utilization, index fragmentation), (f) integration latency (POS events &lt; 30 sec per POS-013, ecommerce sync, banking)
Responsible (R): ERP Admin
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W787_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W787_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W787_Task6" name="SLA compliance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: SLA compliance review: IT Infrastructure Manager reviews SLA compliance: (a) POS uptime vs. 99.9% target per NFR-001, (b) back-office uptime vs. 99.5% target per NFR-002, (c) POS transaction speed vs. &lt; 3 second target per NFR-003, (d) report generation vs. &lt; 30 second target per NFR-004, (e) concurrent users vs. 1,000-1,500 capacity per NFR-005; identify any SLA breaches and root cause
Responsible (R): IT Infra Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W787_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W787_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W787_Task7" name="Performance bottleneck analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Performance bottleneck analysis: For any SLA breaches or degrading trends: (a) ERP Admin analyzes slow queries, long-running batch jobs, and resource contention, (b) DBA reviews database execution plans, index usage, and table growth, (c) identifies root cause: code inefficiency, data volume growth, infrastructure limitation, or configuration issue
Responsible (R): ERP Admin / DBA
Accountable (A): IT Infra Manager
Duration: 2-4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W787_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W787_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W787_Task8" name="Capacity planning update (quarterly)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Capacity planning update (quarterly): IT Infrastructure Manager updates capacity model: (a) current resource utilization (CPU, memory, storage, network), (b) growth rate extrapolation: POS transaction volume growth (~10%/year), new store additions (10-15/year), ecommerce growth (~5–7%/year of revenue), (c) projected resource requirements 6 and 12 months ahead, (d) infrastructure upgrade or scaling plan (cloud auto-scaling, database sharding, caching layer expansion), (e) budget estimate for capacity additions per W373 IT FinOps
Responsible (R): IT Infra Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W787_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W787_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W787_Task9" name="Performance optimization actions">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Performance optimization actions: Based on analysis: (a) database index optimization or rebuild, (b) query tuning for slow reports, (c) batch job scheduling optimization (stagger month-end processing per NFR-015), (d) cache warming for frequently accessed data, (e) infrastructure scaling (add compute, memory, or storage per cloud elasticity)
Responsible (R): ERP Admin / DBA
Accountable (A): IT Infra Manager
Duration: Varies</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W787_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W787_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W787_Task10" name="Monthly IT performance report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly IT performance report: IT Infrastructure Manager prepares report for CIO: (a) SLA compliance dashboard with trend arrows, (b) performance metrics vs. targets, (c) capacity utilization and growth trajectory, (d) optimization actions taken and planned, (e) incident summary (P1-P4 per W595 severity matrix), (f) budget impact of capacity changes
Responsible (R): IT Infra Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W787_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W787_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W787_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W787_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W787_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: IT Infrastructure Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: IT Infrastructure Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
