    <bpmn:process id="W_W831" name="W831. POS Terminal Emergency Swap &amp; Rapid Replacement Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: POS terminal hardware failure during store operating hours; terminal non-responsive despite W265 troubleshooting
Frequency: Weekly; ~5–8 terminal failures/month requiring emergency swap across 600 terminals
Volume: ~5–8 emergency swaps/month; ~1–2 per week; average downtime 30-60 minutes per incident
Owner: IT Helpdesk (Tier 2)
Participants: IT Helpdesk, Store Manager, Cashier, IT Field Technician, POS Vendor Support
Source: workflow W831 — POS Terminal Emergency Swap &amp; Rapid Replacement Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W831_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W831_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W831_Lane2" name="IT Helpdesk Tier 1">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W831_Lane3" name="IT Helpdesk Tier 2">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W831_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W831_Lane5" name="IT Helpdesk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W831_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W831_Start7" name="POS terminal hardware failure during store operating hours; terminal non-responsive…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W831_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W831_Task8" name="Failure report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Failure report: Cashier reports terminal failure to Store Manager: (a) terminal unresponsive after standard troubleshooting per W265 (restart, cable check); (b) Store Manager contacts IT Helpdesk per W48
Responsible (R): Cashier / Store Manager
Accountable (A): IT Helpdesk Lead
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W831_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W831_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W831_Task9" name="Remote diagnosis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Remote diagnosis: IT Helpdesk Tier 1 performs remote diagnosis: (a) check network connectivity; (b) attempt remote restart; (c) check error logs; (d) if confirmed hardware failure: escalate to Tier 2
Responsible (R): IT Helpdesk Tier 1
Accountable (A): IT Helpdesk Lead
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W831_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W831_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W831_Task10" name="Emergency swap authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Emergency swap authorization: IT Helpdesk Tier 2 authorizes emergency swap: (a) confirms hardware failure cannot be resolved remotely; (b) instructs Store Manager to deploy spare terminal from store stock
Responsible (R): IT Helpdesk Tier 2
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W831_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W831_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W831_Task11" name="In-store emergency swap execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: In-store emergency swap execution: Store Manager executes: (a) retrieve spare terminal from secure storage; (b) connect to network and power; (c) system auto-provisions terminal: downloads store-specific configuration per W404 POS hardware master, syncs product master and price file per W533, registers terminal ID on network per W366; (d) verify test transaction; (e) terminal operational
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): IT Helpdesk Tier 2
Duration: 15-30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W831_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W831_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W831_Task12" name="Failed terminal processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Failed terminal processing: (a) Store Manager labels failed terminal with incident ticket number; (b) secures in backroom; (c) IT Helpdesk creates RMA with vendor per W265
Responsible (R): Store Manager / IT Helpdesk
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W831_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W831_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W831_Task13" name="No-spare escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: No-spare escalation: if no spare available at store: (a) IT Helpdesk arranges emergency terminal shipment from nearest IT spare stock (regional hub or neighboring store per W22 store-to-store transfer); (b) expedited delivery within 4-8 hours (metro) or 24-48 hours (provincial); (c) temporary measure: redirect customers to remaining terminals per W526 queue management
Responsible (R): IT Helpdesk / IT Field Technician
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 4-48 hours delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W831_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W831_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W831_Task14" name="Post-incident review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-incident review: (a) IT Helpdesk tracks terminal failure root cause per W378 problem management; (b) vendor RMA resolution per W265; (c) spare stock replenishment per W1544; (d) monthly terminal failure rate analysis per store and by hardware age
Responsible (R): IT Helpdesk / IT Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 30 min/incident + monthly review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W831_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W831_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W831_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W831_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W831_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: IT Helpdesk (Tier 2) review and approval gate
Owner: IT Helpdesk (Tier 2)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
