    <bpmn:process id="W_W1531" name="W1531. Philippine Store WAN Connectivity Monitoring, ISP SLA Management &amp; Failover Testing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous network monitoring alerts; monthly ISP SLA review cycle; quarterly failover testing schedule
Frequency: Real-time monitoring (24/7); monthly SLA review; quarterly failover tests
Volume: 200 store connections + 4 DC connections + HQ = 205 WAN endpoints across Philippines
Owner: IT Network Engineer
Participants: IT Network Engineer, ISP Account Managers, Store Managers, POS System Administrator
Source: workflow W1531 — Philippine Store WAN Connectivity Monitoring, ISP SLA Management &amp; Failover Testing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1531_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1531_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1531_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1531_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1531_Lane2" name="IT Network Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1531_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1531_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1531_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1531_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1531_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1531_Start4" name="Continuous network monitoring alerts; monthly ISP SLA review cycle; quarterly failover…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1531_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1531_Task5" name="Real-time WAN monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Real-time WAN monitoring: (a) IT Network Engineer maintains centralized network monitoring platform (e.g., Nagios, SolarWinds, or cloud-based) tracking: (i) uptime per store connection (ping every 60 seconds), (ii) latency (target: &lt; 100ms to ERP data center), (iii) bandwidth utilization (target: &lt; 70% of provisioned capacity), (iv) packet loss (target: &lt; 0.1%), (v) jitter (target: &lt; 30ms for POS transaction streaming); (b) system generates alerts: (i) Yellow alert: latency &gt; 100ms or packet loss &gt; 0.1% → automatic ISP ticket creation, (ii) Red alert: connection down &gt; 5 min → IT Network Engineer + ISP escalation, Store Manager notified for offline POS mode activation
Responsible (R): System / IT Network Engineer
Accountable (A): IT Operations Manager
Duration: Automated monitoring; 15–30 min/day on alert review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1531_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1531_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1531_Task6" name="ISP SLA tracking and enforcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: ISP SLA tracking and enforcement: (a) IT Network Engineer compiles monthly ISP SLA performance per connection: (i) actual uptime vs. contracted SLA (typically 99.0–99.5% depending on ISP and location), (ii) total downtime minutes, (iii) number of outage incidents, (iv) mean time to repair (MTTR) per incident; (b) identifies SLA breaches: uptime below contracted threshold → IT Network Engineer files SLA credit claim with ISP per contract terms; (c) quarterly: IT Network Engineer reviews ISP performance across all 205 connections and presents to IT Operations Manager: (i) top 10 worst-performing stores (by uptime), (ii) ISP comparison (if multiple ISPs used), (iii) recommendation: upgrade connection, change ISP, or add backup connection for worst-performing stores
Responsible (R): IT Network Engineer
Accountable (A): IT Operations Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1531_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1531_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1531_Task7" name="Failover testing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Failover testing (quarterly): (a) IT Network Engineer schedules quarterly failover test for each store: (i) simulate primary WAN failure (disable primary connection), (ii) verify: automatic failover to backup connection activates (if store has dual WAN), OR POS switches to offline mode (stores without backup connection), (iii) verify: POS local data store continues processing transactions, (iv) verify: upon primary restoration, queued transactions sync to ERP without data loss; (b) document results per store: failover activation time (target: &lt; 30 seconds for dual WAN, immediate for offline POS mode), data integrity (zero transaction loss); (c) stores that fail failover test: IT Network Engineer remediates (router configuration, backup ISP activation, POS offline mode tuning) and retests within 2 weeks
Responsible (R): IT Network Engineer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): IT Operations Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/store/test × 200 stores = ~33–50 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1531_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1531_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1531_Task8" name="ISP escalation and incident management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: ISP escalation and incident management: (a) when ISP outage occurs: (i) IT Network Engineer opens priority ticket with ISP (via ISP portal or hotline), (ii) tracks resolution progress, (iii) for outages &gt; 4 hours: escalates to ISP account manager and IT Operations Manager, (iv) for outages &gt; 24 hours: escalates to VP IT and evaluates emergency backup connectivity options (e.g., temporary 4G/5G router, satellite internet); (b) post-incident: documents root cause, resolution time, and preventive measures in incident management system per PA-27.1 (Service Management)
Responsible (R): IT Network Engineer
Accountable (A): IT Operations Manager
Duration: Per incident: 30 min – 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1531_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1531_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1531_Task9" name="Annual connectivity planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual connectivity planning: (a) IT Network Engineer and IT Operations Manager review: (i) bandwidth sufficiency (are store connections keeping up with growing POS transaction volume and ecommerce order volume?), (ii) ISP contract renewals (negotiate better rates or SLA based on 2–3 years of performance data), (iii) new store connectivity requirements (ensure ISP provisioning is in the new store opening timeline per PA-20.2), (iv) technology upgrades (fiber where available, 4G/5G backup for critical stores, satellite for remote island stores); (b) presents connectivity plan and budget to VP IT for approval
Responsible (R): IT Network Engineer / IT Operations Manager
Accountable (A): VP IT
Duration: 2–3 weeks/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1531_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1531_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1531_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1531_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1531_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: IT Network Engineer review and approval gate
Owner: IT Network Engineer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1531_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1531_Annotation11" targetRef="W1531_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
