    <bpmn:process id="W_W1544" name="W1544. POS Terminal Lifecycle Management, Hardware Refresh Cycle &amp; Peripheral Standardization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Hardware refresh cycle (POS terminals replaced every 5 years); or terminal failure beyond repair; or new store opening (W16); or peripheral upgrade (e.g., new barcode scanner model)
Frequency: ~120 terminal replacements/year (600 terminals ÷ 5-year lifecycle); ~30–50 peripheral replacements/year
Volume: 600 POS terminals across 200 stores; 3 terminals per store
Owner: IT Infrastructure Manager
Participants: IT Infrastructure Manager, IT Asset Coordinator, Store Manager, POS vendor
Source: workflow W1544 — POS Terminal Lifecycle Management, Hardware Refresh Cycle &amp; Peripheral Standardization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1544_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1544_Lane1" name="IT Infrastructure Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1544_Lane2" name="IT Asset Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1544_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1544_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1544_Start5" name="Hardware refresh cycle (POS terminals replaced every 5 years); or terminal failure beyond…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1544_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1544_Task6" name="Lifecycle planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Lifecycle planning: IT Infrastructure Manager maintains POS hardware asset register — terminal serial number, store assignment, installation date, warranty expiry, firmware version, last maintenance date; system identifies terminals approaching end-of-life (Year 4+) for proactive replacement scheduling
Responsible (R): IT Infrastructure Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1544_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1544_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1544_Task7" name="Hardware refresh procurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Hardware refresh procurement: IT Infrastructure Manager initiates annual POS hardware refresh RFP — specifies minimum terminal specifications (processor, RAM, storage, touchscreen, offline capability per POS-002), peripheral compatibility, vendor support SLA, Philippine service center availability; Procurement processes purchase per W21/W2
Responsible (R): IT Infrastructure Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 40 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1544_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1544_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1544_Task8" name="Peripheral standardization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Peripheral standardization: IT Infrastructure Manager defines standard peripheral kit per terminal — barcode scanner model (1D+2D), receipt printer model (thermal, BIR-registered), cash drawer, customer-facing display, POS terminal model; publishes approved hardware list to IT asset management; any deviation requires IT Infrastructure Manager approval
Responsible (R): IT Infrastructure Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 8 hours/year (updates)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1544_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1544_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1544_Task9" name="Staging &amp; configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Staging &amp; configuration: New terminals received at HQ IT staging area — IT Asset Coordinator images each terminal with standard POS software, configures store-specific settings (location code, printer mapping, offline cache), registers with MDM (W371), tests peripheral connectivity, applies security hardening; staged terminal assigned to specific store and terminal position
Responsible (R): IT Asset Coordinator
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/terminal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1544_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1544_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1544_Task10" name="Swarm replacement execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Swarm replacement execution: For scheduled refreshes, IT sends replacement terminals to stores in batches (regional approach); Store Manager coordinates swap — install new terminal during off-peak hours, verify connectivity, test transaction processing, confirm offline mode functionality; return old terminal to HQ via reverse logistics
Responsible (R): Store Manager / IT Asset Coordinator
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/terminal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1544_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1544_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1544_Task11" name="Old terminal disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Old terminal disposition: Returned terminals assessed at HQ — (a) refurbishable units (Year 3–4, still functional): cleaned, reimaged, held as hot spares for emergency replacement; (b) non-refurbishable units: data wipe per security standards, asset disposal per W39 with IT asset vendor, BIR permit update for decommissioned terminal; IT Asset Coordinator updates asset register
Responsible (R): IT Asset Coordinator
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Manager
Duration: 30 min/terminal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1544_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1544_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1544_Task12" name="Emergency terminal replacement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Emergency terminal replacement: For terminal failures during business hours, Store Manager reports to IT helpdesk (W48); IT dispatches hot spare from nearest regional spare pool via same-day courier; Store Manager swaps terminal; failed unit returned to HQ for repair assessment; target: replacement terminal delivered within 24 hours
Responsible (R): Store Manager / IT Helpdesk
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Manager
Duration: 30 min (store) + 24 hours (delivery)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1544_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1544_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1544_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1544_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1544_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: IT Infrastructure Manager review and approval gate
Owner: IT Infrastructure Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1544_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1544_Annotation14" targetRef="W1544_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
