    <bpmn:process id="W_W5520" name="W5520. Core Network Services &amp; IPAM (DNS/DHCP/IP-Schema) Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New or moved site requiring IP-schema allocation (VS-37); DNS/DHCP change request approved via W1409; DHCP scope-utilization alert; or the quarterly IPAM reconciliation
Frequency: Per change; continuous scope-utilization monitoring; quarterly reconciliation; annual NTP audit
Volume: 205+ sites; ~2,500 endpoints; ~200+ SD-WAN nodes (W366); 4 internal DNS zones; ~15 core-service changes/month
Owner: IT Infrastructure Manager
Participants: Network Engineers, IT Security Manager, IT Asset Manager (W3233 CMDB), Application Manager, Store Managers (site access for surveys)
Source: workflow W5520 — Core Network Services &amp; IPAM (DNS/DHCP/IP-Schema) Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5520_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5520_Lane1" name="Network Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5520_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5520_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5520_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5520_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5520_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5520_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5520_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5520_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5520_Start3" name="New or moved site requiring IP-schema allocation (VS-37); DNS/DHCP change request…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5520_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5520_Task4" name="IP-schema governance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: IP-schema governance: Allocate site/subnet addressing from the enterprise IP plan for new/moved sites (VS-37) and DC/network redesigns (links to W366; IT/OT zone boundaries stay in VS-190 scope per W5418)
Responsible (R): Network Engineer
Accountable (A): IT Infra Mgr
Duration: 1 hour/site event × ~10/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5520_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5520_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5520_Task5" name="Internal DNS lifecycle">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Internal DNS lifecycle: Zone/record changes via W1409-approved requests; split-horizon records for internal services; public-zone records coordinated with the domain portfolio (W377)
Responsible (R): Network Engineer
Accountable (A): IT Infra Mgr
Duration: 30 min/change × ~15/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5520_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5520_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5520_Task6" name="DHCP scope &amp; lease management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: DHCP scope &amp; lease management: Scope sizing vs utilization alerts; redundant DHCP pairs for DC/HQ; store-scope templates pushed with the SD-WAN site template (W366)
Responsible (R): Network Engineer
Accountable (A): IT Infra Lead
Duration: 1 hour/month review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5520_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5520_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5520_Task7" name="Time-sync (NTP) baseline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Time-sync (NTP) baseline: Authenticated NTP hierarchy keeping POS/receipt timestamps coherent (BIR CAS requirement); annual audit of drift &amp; source authentication
Responsible (R): Network Engineer
Accountable (A): IT Security Mgr
Duration: 8 hours/year audit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5520_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5520_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5520_Task8" name="Quarterly IPAM reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly IPAM reconciliation: Compare the IPAM register against W3233 discovery data; clean stale records; feed corrections to the CMDB
Responsible (R): Network Engineer / IT Asset Mgr
Accountable (A): IT Infra Mgr
Duration: 3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5520_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5520_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5520_Task9" name="Core-service change control">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Core-service change control: All DNS/DHCP core changes ride W1409 with a rollback plan; the emergency path is documented and post-reviewed
Responsible (R): Network Engineer / IT Change Mgr
Accountable (A): IT Infra Mgr
Duration: Administrative</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5520_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5520_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5520_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5520_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5520_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: core DNS/DHCP changes require W1409 approval with a rollback plan | - operational: quarterly IPAM-to-CMDB reconciliation gate before schema exceptions are accepted
Owner: IT Infrastructure Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5520_Assoc12" sourceRef="W5520_Annotation11" targetRef="W5520_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5520_Flow13" sourceRef="W5520_Start3" targetRef="W5520_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5520_Flow14" sourceRef="W5520_Task4" targetRef="W5520_Task5" />
