    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5573" name="W5573. Server-Room &amp; Data-Center Environmental Event Response (Cooling Failure, Water Intrusion, Fire-Suppression Discharge)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: An environmental failure inside a server room, data hall, or network room: precision-cooling (CRAC/CRAH) failure with rising rack-inlet temperature, water leak over or adjacent to racks, fire-suppression discharge or fault (clean-agent release or pre-action trip), smoke/heat event, or a UPS-room thermal excursion
Frequency: ~2–6 minor events per year chain-wide across the HQ server room, the 4 DC IT rooms, and network rooms (single-CRAC trips and small leaks dominate); a full-cooling loss or suppression discharge is the rare tail
Volume: 1 event × the affected hall/room (a network room to ~100+ racks) × the thermal-runaway window (minutes to a few hours before inlet thresholds breach) × the failover decision boundary against W55&#x27;s RTO
Owner: IT Infrastructure Manager; ITOC Lead (detection through the W380 monitoring canon)
Participants: CIO, Data Center facility vendor, Landlord/base-building Facilities (VS-138), W55 failover execution team, Application/platform owners, Security Guard, HSE Manager (W140 where injury), VS-26 insurance (W876-class equipment claim), Fire-protection contractor (BFP-certified)
Source: workflow W5573 — Server-Room &amp; Data-Center Environmental Event Response (Cooling Failure, Water Intrusion, Fire-Suppression Discharge)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5573_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5573_Lane1" name="ITOC Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5573_Lane2" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5573_Lane3" name="IT Infrastructure">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5573_Lane4" name="Platform owners">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5573_Lane5" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5573_Lane6" name="IT Infrastructure Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5573_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5573_Start8" name="An environmental failure inside a server room, data hall, or network room…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5573_Task9" name="Detect &amp; classify">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Detect &amp; classify: the W380 alert path opens the event; classify by class — cooling (inlet trend vs threshold), water (leak-detection rail or visual), suppression (discharge/fault), smoke/heat; the class sets the Step-2/3 sequence
Responsible (R): ITOC Lead
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Manager
Duration: 2–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5573_Task10" name="Life safety &amp; access">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Life safety &amp; access: smoke or suppression discharge evacuates the room immediately — two-person rule for all re-entry; nobody enters during agent hold or where heat/smoke persists; injury response per W501/W140
Responsible (R): Security Guard / ITOC
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5573_Task11" name="Stabilize the environment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Stabilize the environment: cooling class — portable cooling in, airflow sealed, load shed to non-critical racks; water class — isolate the source, de-energize the affected PDUs/bus before water reaches live parts, contained/extracted; suppression class — hold the clear, contractor called for re-arm before any restart
Responsible (R): IT Infrastructure / DC facility vendor
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Manager
Duration: 15 min–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5573_Task12" name="Protect data">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Protect data: graceful-shutdown order executed for racks trending past threshold (database and transaction systems last-stated first); backup currency verified per W382 before protective shutdowns
Responsible (R): Platform owners / IT Infrastructure
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 15–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5573_Task13" name="Failover boundary decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Failover boundary decision: if the credible repair window exceeds the service RTO, W55 failover execution is triggered with the declaration; otherwise degraded-mode notices ride W659/W535-class store impacts; the decision and its basis are logged either way
Responsible (R): CIO / W55 execution team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: At threshold breach</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5573_Task14" name="Vendor remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Vendor remediation: chiller/CRAC emergency callout (DC facility vendor; base-building side via VS-138 SLA), plumbing/roof source repair where water entered, fire-protection contractor re-arms and certifies the suppression system (BFP-certified)
Responsible (R): IT Infrastructure / VS-138 Facilities
Accountable (A): IT Infrastructure Manager
Duration: Hours–days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5573_Task15" name="Validation &amp; staged repower">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Validation &amp; staged repower: room re-entry only after thermal/humidity and leak checks pass and the suppression system is certified armed; repower is staged (PDUs, then storage, then compute) with application health checks per layer; degraded modes lifted
Responsible (R): IT Infrastructure / Platform owners
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5573_Task16" name="After-action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: After-action: problem-management RCA per W378 (root cause, monitoring gap, capacity result), lessons to the W856-class review, equipment-damage claim to VS-26 where applicable, and a W376 capacity/capex note where cooling headroom was the cause
Responsible (R): IT Infrastructure Manager / ITOC Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5573_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5573_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5573_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5573_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-323 (ensure controlled execution — Infrastructure &amp; Platform (PA-27.2).) | - operational: failover-boundary decisions logged with their RTO basis; repower only after the documented suppression/leak/thermal checks; RCAs tracked to the capacity process
Owner: IT Infrastructure Manager; ITOC Lead (detection through the W380 monitoring canon)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5573_Assoc19" sourceRef="W5573_Annotation18" targetRef="W5573_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
